# rule.require.commit-scopes

every commit carries a scope: `type(scope): message` — the scope locates the change (module, feature, domain), groups the changelog, speeds review
👍 `fix(invoice): handle negative line items` · `feat(auth): add oauth provider` · `chore(deps): bump typescript to 5.4`
👎 `fix: handle negative line items`
enforcement: commit with no scope = blocker

